---
/**
 * The mascot, second generation, in a page (D17.1 to D17.25; docs/discovery/PLAN-TORTUE.md).
 *
 * The drawing is read from the very file the editor validated (design/mascot/v2/mascot.svg):
 * the fingerprint her sheet is dated on is the fingerprint of what ships. This component writes
 * nothing but attributes on it, and brings the two stylesheets that turn them into what is
 * seen — hers, and the six tints the player may give her flamingo, which no other page of the
 * site receives.
 *
 * She is decoration to assistive technology (aria-hidden in the file): whatever she does is
 * said in words by the button that holds her and by the status line of the game.
 *
 * She lives in the game block only (D17.9): never near the question field, a result of the
 * search, the sheet of « Demander », a section page, the preview card or the favicon.
 *
 * Imported by src/components/Game2.astro alone, which the home page imports only in a build of
 * the second generation (`__CEL_MASCOT2__`): a build of the first carries not a byte of her.
 */
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import '../styles/mascot2-tokens.css';
import '../styles/mascot2.css';
import { mascotMarkup } from '../lib/mascot2.ts';

// As she is before a word is found: the turtle. The script gives her the look the game
// remembers; without script she stays as she is here.
const drawing = readFileSync('design/mascot/v2/mascot.svg', 'utf8').trim();
const markup = mascotMarkup(drawing, { state: 0 });
---

<Fragment set:html={markup} />
